@startuml
/' mkl fixture. Copyright 2026 kingle.zhuang. '/
' DS-07 - Sequence diagram for CU-07 Register incident
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Requester" as ACT_Requester
boundary "Incident Form" as B_Form
entity "Requester" as E_Requester
entity "Category" as E_Category
entity "ServiceAgreement" as E_Agreement
entity "Incident" as E_Incident
participant "DeadlinePolicy" as S_Policy

ACT_Requester -> B_Form : describe the problem
note right of B_Form
  Design decision supporting RNF-01 / CP-05:
  capture registrationDate once from the server clock.
  Use that same value for due-date calculation and incident registration.
  CU-07 / CA-01 / CP-06: identifier() exposes the Incident's business referenceNumber.
end note
B_Form -> E_Category : exists()
alt FA-02 category does not exist
  E_Category --> B_Form : unknown category
  B_Form --> ACT_Requester : report unknown category; no incident registered
else valid category
  B_Form -> E_Requester : isAuthorizedFor(category)
  alt FA-01 requester is not authorized
    E_Requester --> B_Form : reason for rejection
    B_Form --> ACT_Requester : report authorization rejection; no incident registered
  else authorized requester
    B_Form -> E_Category : currentAgreement()
    E_Category -> E_Agreement : isCurrent()
    B_Form -> S_Policy : calculateDueDate(agreement, registrationDate)
    S_Policy -> E_Agreement : deadlineHours()
    B_Form -> E_Incident : register(description, requester, category, registrationDate, dueDate)
    B_Form -> E_Incident : identifier()
    B_Form --> ACT_Requester : show incident identifier and dueDate
  end
end
@enduml
